    "abstract": "Parts list for the longitudinal skin joint of the aft lower shell, listing the aluminium inner doubler with the interim sealing standard call-out and the edging grommet that closes the new drain path.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure identifies the detail parts of the longitudinal skin joint of the aft lower shell between stations C52 and C66, including the inner doubler, the joint angle and the drain grommet installation.",
      "figure_note": "Sheet 1 shows the left-hand joint; the right-hand joint is symmetric. Fastener quantities are per joint, not per aircraft. Item 80 is fitted only at the four drain positions shown on sheet 2 and is timed with the production cut-in of the interim sealing standard, not with the retrofit bulletin; a joint at the earlier standard has no grommet and no drain hole. The interim sealant is called out on the installation drawing and remains an unlisted material."
    },
