    "abstract": "Parts list for the longitudinal skin joint of the aft lower shell, listing the aluminium and the titanium inner doubler as alternates against the corrosion-resistant doubler modification standard.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure identifies the detail parts of the longitudinal skin joint of the aft lower shell between stations C52 and C66, including the inner doubler and the drain grommet installation.",
      "figure_note": "Item 10 and item 10A are alternates and must be selected against the embodiment standard of the aircraft: item 10 is the titanium doubler with the machined drain relief and item 10A is the earlier aluminium item. The two are not interchangeable and a joint must carry one standard throughout. The grommet quantity follows the doubler: four positions with item 10A, twelve with item 10, because the machined relief drains every bay rather than only the four low points. Sheet 1 shows the left-hand joint; the right-hand joint is symmetric. Fastener quantities are per joint, not per aircraft."
    },
